<!-- HJCD-IK sphere model "iiwa14" for csrc/urdf/iiwa14.urdf (the preset's end-effector frame is iiwa_joint_ee).
     Produced by GRiD 0.6.0: `grid-spherize iiwa14.urdf -\-resolution 0.03 -\-mesh-mode bounded-bulge` on Drake's
     iiwa14_spheres_dense_collision.urdf, whose collision geometry is already a sphere model (BSD-3-Clause, Drake /
     iiwa_stack); the spherizer passes those 46 spheres through. Base-chain spheres (iiwa_link_0) are dropped at bake.
     Fidelity (grid-spherize -\-report, sampled, 2000 surface points per link; not a coverage certificate):
       against Drake's collision geometry: bulge_max 1.8-2.2 mm, uncovered 0.0 % on every link;
       against the visual meshes (-\-geometry visual):
         link   spheres bulge_max_mm bulge_p99_mm uncovered_%
         link_0   4      92.5          85.0        5.8
         link_1   5      70.5          64.0       54.2
         link_2   9      95.0          81.8        0.3
         link_3   9      76.2          59.5        1.6
         link_4   6      74.3          65.1        6.8
         link_5   9      34.9          31.3       15.2
         link_6   3      44.0          41.1       18.3
         link_7   1      49.0          47.9        0.0
     Drake's model is conservative and sparse against the visual shell; a tighter bounded-bulge model from the mesh
     collision geometry is a follow-up (GRiD ask V4 covers the cylinder end caps of the primitive variant). -->
